<title>GERMANY: Villeroy &amp; Boch proposes no dividend payout for 96.</title>
<headline>Villeroy &amp; Boch proposes no dividend payout for 96.</headline>
<dateline>METTLACH, Germany 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German bathroom fittings and tableware maker Villeroy &amp; Boch said on Friday it had proposed paying no dividend in 1996 and said it expected a loss in 1996 as restructuring costs hit earnings.</p>
<p>Villeroy said that group sales fell by two percent in 1996 to 1.453 billion marks.</p>
